{"date": "2026-10-11", "rank": 2, "topic": "環境", "title": "Why Ireland Imports Most of Its Fruit and Vegetables", "level": "B2", "summaryZh": "愛爾蘭超過八成蔬果仰賴進口，本地菜農從600戶減至不到70戶。", "sources": [{"name": "The Irish Times", "url": "https://www.irishtimes.com/environment/2026/10/10/why-doesnt-ireland-grow-more-veg/"}], "paragraphs": ["Ireland imports most of the fruit and vegetables it eats. According to the Climate Change Advisory Council, around 83 per cent of the fresh produce consumed in the country comes from abroad. Some of this is unavoidable, since crops such as bananas and oranges simply cannot be grown in the Irish climate.", "The number of commercial vegetable growers has also fallen sharply. In the 1990s there were more than 600; today there are fewer than 70. However, production has not dropped at the same rate, because the industry is now concentrated in a small number of large, specialised farms.", "Growers face several challenges. This summer was the hottest on record, and research by Teagasc found that crops without irrigation lost between a quarter and two-fifths of their yield. Labour accounts for more than 40 per cent of costs, and many farmers struggle to find workers or someone to take over the business.", "There are some signs of support. Six supermarkets have signed a charter promising longer contracts with growers, and experts suggest that new technology, such as robotics, could reduce the need for manual work."], "gloss": {"a": {"zh": "一個", "pos": "art.", "base": "a", "hi": "एक", "en": "one; any (article)", "es": "un; una", "lvl": "A1"}, "abroad": {"zh": "國外", "pos": "adv.", "base": "abroad", "hi": "विदेश में", "en": "in or from another country", "es": "en el extranjero", "lvl": "B1"}, "according": {"zh": "根據（according to）", "pos": "adv.", "base": "according", "hi": "के अनुसार (according to)", "en": "as stated by (according to)", "es": "según (according to)", "lvl": "B1"}, "accounts": {"zh": "佔（account for：佔…比例）", "pos": "v.", "base": "account", "n